From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: bound the scan result frame to its message

rwnx_rx_scanu_result_ind() takes ind->length from the device as the
length of the beacon or probe response in ind->payload and does not check
it against the message. A length past the message makes
cfg80211_inform_bss() read behind the buffer. A length below the probe
response header makes ielen wrap to a huge size_t, and the handler also
writes the timestamp into that header.

Require the frame to fit in msg->param_len (clamped to the received frame
by rwnx_rx_handle_msg()) and to hold the probe response header.
Otherwise drop the result and count it in rx_bad_frame_drops.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
index a52adc6..dd7ff5e 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -766,7 +766,18 @@ static inline int rwnx_rx_scanu_result_ind(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw,
 
 
     RWNX_DBG(RWNX_FN_ENTRY_STR);
-	
+
+    /* ind->length is the frame length from the device. The frame must lie
+     * inside the message, and it must hold the probe response header:
+     * the timestamp is written into it and ielen is length minus that
+     * header (a shorter frame made ielen wrap to a huge size_t). */
+    if (msg->param_len < offsetof(struct scanu_result_ind, payload) ||
+        len > msg->param_len - offsetof(struct scanu_result_ind, payload) ||
+        len < offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.probe_resp.variable)) {
+        rx_bad_frame_drops++;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     chan = ieee80211_get_channel(rwnx_hw->wiphy, ind->center_freq);
 
     if (chan != NULL) {
